---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
import "../styles/global.css";
import H1 from "../components/H1.astro";
import Paragraph from "../components/Paragraph.astro";
import { Markdown } from "@astropub/md";

const changelogContent = `
## 1.3.3 - January 16, 2026

- Integrated Sentry to detect possible crashes and errors.

---

## 1.3.2 - January 15, 2026

- The compression quality of PNG and SVG files has been improved.
- Some crashes in macOS 14 have been fixed, especially for new users.
- Other minor fixes.

---

## v1.3.1 - December 26, 2025

- Clear error messages when switching between compress/convert modes.
- The app now starts in the background when launched at login with "Keep in Menu Bar" enabled.
- Improve images compression.
- Fixed video compression not reducing file sizes and improved encoding performance.

---

## v1.3.0 - December 15, 2025

- I watched folders and added hot folder monitoring.
- You can now use Picmal with the Shortcuts app.
- Picmal runs in the background when you log in.
- Compress output it's available for images, audios and videos.

---

## v1.2.9 - December 10, 2025

- Persist files when switching between the 'Convert' and 'Compress' tabs.
- Add support for dragging and dropping files onto the dock icon.
- Fixed an issue with SVG compression that was failing because it could not interpret some CSS classes correctly.
- HIF format support (Canon HEIF) was added.
- Fixed DNG/RAW rotation issue.

---

## v1.2.8 - November 30, 2025

- Presets for audio and video conversion.
- Support for converting HEIC to WebP.
- You can now strip the metadata from audio, video and image files.
- Output file displays the settings used.
- Parts of the code have been rewritten to improve stability and reliability.
- The Preferences menu has been reorganised for better usability.
- Issues resulting in unusable files during MKV to MP4 conversions when certain codecs were used have been resolved.

---

## v1.2.7 - November 20, 2025

- PDF results look clearer and sharper.
- You can now open files from the top menu using File > Open or with the shortcut Command O.
- Picmal now understands folders. Drop a folder and it will gather everything inside, including subfolders, ready to convert.
- On the Finder context menu you will now see new options to convert or compress images with Picmal.

<video autoplay muted loop width="100%" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
  <source src="images/changelog/1.2.7/drop_folder.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
  Your browser does not support the video tag.
</video>

---

## v1.2.6 - November 16, 2025

- Color space conversion: Convert images to sRGB, Display P3, Adobe RGB, ProPhoto RGB, Rec. 709, or Rec. 2020 with proper ICC profile embedding.
- View color space info for converted images via a new clickable icon in the Size column.
- Fixed FLAC to AAC audio conversion issues in optimized advanced mode.

![Auto mode enabled](/images/changelog/1.2.6/color_space_info.png)
![Auto mode enabled](/images/changelog/1.2.6/convert_color_space.png)

---

## v1.2.5 - November 15, 2025

- Conversion from EPS to SVG has been added.
- Conversion from AI to SVG added.

---

## v1.2.4 - November 13, 2025

- You can now see the conversion speed percentage, along with an estimated time remaining, for videos and audio files.
- You can now experience significant performance improvements: Video conversions are much faster and use less memory, especially for long files. Instant conversion (no re-encoding) works for 50+ format combinations including WebM, MKV, MP4, FLV, 3GP, and more.
- You can now use VideoToolbox's H.264 hardware encoding for over 12 video formats on Apple Silicon, offering a speed boost of 10–50x for FLV, WMV, MPEG, 3GP, WTV, F4V and MXF.
- WebM codec compatibility in Advanced mode has been fixed (now properly enforces VP8/VP9/AV1 codecs).
- The issue where buttons (metadata, progress info, Show in Finder) were not clickable during conversion has been fixed.
- PDF compression is now faster and more accurate.

![Auto mode enabled](/images/changelog/1.2.4/video_progress.png)

---

## v1.2.3 - November 12, 2025

- Fixed bug where multi-select functionality was broken for audio and video files. Format dropdown now properly populates when selecting media files via checkbox.
- Fixed compression savings showing incorrect percentages when converting between formats.

---

## v1.2.2 - November 04, 2025

- Fixed the non-clickable checkbox in Advanced mode.
- Added Advanced mode to both Conversion and Compression modes.
- Fixed the bottom tab bar so that it now truncates text when there is too much.
- Some PDF compression errors that were not working well have been fixed.
- Progress has been added to the compression and conversion of files to improve the user experience. Sometimes, compressing long files can take more than 2–3 minutes, and users thought it was stuck.
- A "Cancel" button has been added while converting/compressing to allow you to stop the process.

---

## v1.2.1 - November 01, 2025

- Batch resize images with 5 flexible modes (percentage, fixed, max dimensions, width/height-only).
- Display metadata for audio and video files (duration, bitrate, codec, sample rate).
- Advanced mode for audio and video with enhanced FFmpeg controls.
- Fixed PDF compression corrupting colors in Keynote/PowerPoint presentations.
- Compressed files now automatically include "\\_compressed" suffix.
- Improved format support (31 audio, 25 video formats).

---

## v1.2.0 - October 30, 2025

<video autoplay muted loop width="100%" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
  <source src="/picmal-1.2.0-demo.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
  Your browser does not support the video tag.
</video>

- Support audio formats: MP3, WAV, AAC, M4A, FLAC, OGG, OGA, WMA, OPUS, M4R, AC3, WV, FSSD, AU, SPH, GSRT, CVS, CVSD, CAF, SPX, IRCAM, SND, CVU, VOC, VMS, PRC, AMB, DTS, TTA, 8SVX, DVMS, SNDR, VOX, SD2, HTK, SOU, W64, SLN, TXW, SMP, RA, SNDT, HCOM, FAP, CDDA, PAF, MAUD, MP2, WVE, NIST, AIFF, AIF, AIFC, AVR, IMA, PVF.
- Support video formats: MP4, MOV, AVI, MKV, WEBM, FLV, WMV, M4V, MPG, MPEG, 3GP, M2TS, MTS, VOB, ASF, OGV, WTV, TS, MJPEG, M2V, HEVC, F4V, MXF.

---

## v1.1.9 - October 29, 2025

- 18 new formats now support conversion: JP2, PICT, QTIF, SGI, TGA, JXL, DDS, EXR, PBM, PGM, PPM, PNM,PCX, XBM, XPM, QOI, PSD.
- 10 new formats now support compression: BMP, JP2, TGA, JXL, DDS, EXR, PCX, SGI, QOI.

---

## v1.1.8 - October 25, 2025

- Small fixes

---

## v1.1.7 - October 23, 2025

- Small fixes

---

## v1.1.6 - October 23, 2025

- Fixed a crash that occurred when using the drag-and-drop view.

---

## v1.1.5 - October 20, 2025

- Performance has been improved.
- PDFs now convert every page, not just the first one.
- SVG compression is now available.
- I fixed a crash that happened when you dragged and dropped something.
- Compression presets: You can choose from six different compression settings (maximum quality, high quality, balanced, web optimised, social media, maximum compression) or make your own custom settings.

---

## v1.1.4 - October 12, 2025

- Enhanced conversion and compression performance.

---

## v1.1.3 - October 11, 2025

- **License activation required:** Starting from this version, you'll need to activate your license within the app. Retrieve your license key from [app.lemonsqueezy.com/my-orders](https://app.lemonsqueezy.com/my-orders) and activate it via **Picmal → Register License…**

---

## v1.1.2 - October 3, 2025

- Small fixes and performant improvements.

## v1.1.1 - September 29, 2025

- Fixed compression output: Resolved issue where files were not being compressed correctly in the output when compression settings were enabled.
- Auto Compress Mode: Enable automatic compression on file drop! Turn on "Auto compress mode" in **Preferences → Files**, then simply drag files into compress mode - compression begins instantly without needing to press any buttons. Perfect for streamlined batch processing workflows.
- Custom file naming for compression: Added prefix and suffix options for compressed output files. Configure custom naming in **Preferences → Output**, or leave fields blank to overwrite original files.
- Added **"Clear settings"** button to reset all compression quality settings to defaults.

![Auto mode enabled](/images/changelog/1.1.1/auto_mode.png)

---

## v1.1.0 - September 23, 2025

- **New compress mode:** Directly reduce the size of JPG, WebP, PNG, GIF, TIFF, AVIF, and PDF files without converting them first
- **Option to compress images after converting:** Compress images after converting them to JPG, WebP, PNG, GIF, TIFF, AVIF, or PDF
- **Minor improvements and bug fixes:** Various small fixes to improve overall app reliability

![Compress mode available](/images/changelog/1.1.0/main_compress_mode.png)

---

## v1.0.9 - September 21, 2025

- **Fixed default format conversion storage:** Resolved an issue where default format conversion settings were not being stored properly in some cases
- **General stability improvements:** Various small fixes to improve overall app reliability

---

## v1.0.8 - September 11, 2025

- Added batch output format selection to apply a single format to multiple files at once.
- Added notifications when file conversions are complete.

### Major improvements

#### Batch output format selection

![Batch outuput format selection feature](/images/changelog/1.0.8/multiple_output_update.png)

Apply a single format to multiple files at once. There is no need to set the format for each file individually anymore. Select multiple files and apply one output format to all of them at once to save time and clicks.

#### Conversion notifications

![Notifications active](/images/changelog/1.0.8/notifications_picmal.png)

Picmal will now notify you when your files have finished converting. Whether you're working on a single file or a batch, you'll get a quick alert so you can move on to the next task without constantly checking.

![Conversion complete notification](/images/changelog/1.0.8/notification_complete.png)

---

## v1.0.7 - September 10, 2025

### What's new in v1.0.7

- **Default output formats:** Set preferred formats once and automatically use them for every drag & drop
- **Dark mode:** Switch to dark mode for comfortable viewing, especially on fully dark Mac setups
- **Improved settings UI:** Redesigned settings menu with cleaner, more intuitive interface
- **Seamless updates:** Continue using the built-in update system or download from Gumroad

### Major improvements

#### Set and forget conversion formats

![Default format conversion settings](/images/changelog/1.0.7/default_format.png)

No more selecting output formats every single time. Set your preferred formats once in the settings, and Picmal will automatically apply them to every file you drag and drop. Perfect for users who consistently convert to the same formats.

#### Dark mode for comfortable viewing

![Dark mode interface](/images/changelog/1.0.7/dark_mode.png)

If you're running your Mac in dark mode, you'll appreciate this addition. No more "nuclear white blasting in your face" when opening Picmal. Simply go to **Settings > General** and choose your preferred appearance mode.

![Dark mode setting](/images/changelog/1.0.7/dark_mode_setting.png)

#### Enhanced settings experience

The settings menu has been redesigned with a cleaner, more intuitive interface. This is the foundation for upcoming features, making it easier to navigate and configure Picmal as new options are added.

### How to get the update

You can download v1.0.7 in two ways:

- Use the built-in "Check for Updates" feature inside your Picmal app
- Download directly from Gumroad as usual

### Looking ahead

#### Your feedback matters

Have ideas for Picmal's future? Send them to support@picmal.app. User feedback continues to drive development priorities and feature decisions.

#### Continued development

With the improved settings foundation in place, expect more configuration options and features in upcoming releases. The redesigned interface makes it easier to add new settings without cluttering the user experience.

---

## v1.0.6 - August 28, 2025

### What's new in v1.0.6

- **Built-in update system:** Check for and install updates directly from the app without visiting Gumroad
- **Bug fixes:** Resolved conversion issues affecting EPS, AI, and WebP formats
- **Error reporting system:** Automatic error detection to help improve app stability (no personal data collected)
- **New website:** Picmal now has a dedicated home at [picmal.app](https://picmal.app)

### Major improvements

#### Seamless updates

No more manual downloads from Gumroad or waiting for email notifications that might end up in spam. Simply go to Preferences and click "Check for Updates" to get the latest version instantly.

#### Format conversion fixes

Fixed critical bugs that were affecting several image format conversions, particularly EPS, AI, and WebP files. These formats should now convert reliably without errors.

#### Proactive error detection

A new error-reporting system has been implemented to identify and resolve issues faster. This system:

- Does not collect personal data or device information
- Only analyzes errors to improve app stability
- Helps prevent future conversion problems

### Looking ahead

#### Upcoming features

The next major update will focus on:

- **Default conversion settings:** Set preferred output formats (e.g., always convert PNG to WebP)
- **Batch format changes:** Select multiple images and change output formats all at once
- **Homebrew installation:** Install and update Picmal via Homebrew (coming soon)

#### Licensing system

A new licensing system is in development to replace Gumroad dependency. Current users will receive their licenses via email with no interruption to service.

---

## v1.0.5 - July 21, 2025

### What's New in v1.0.5

- **Custom file naming:** You can now add custom prefixes and suffixes to your converted images. Perfect for organizing batches or adding timestamps to your files.
- **Image metadata display:** View detailed metadata information for your images directly in Picmal, including EXIF data, color profiles, and file properties.

### How to use these features

#### Adding prefixes and suffixes

In the conversion settings, you'll find new options to add text before (prefix) or after (suffix) your image filenames. This is especially useful when processing large batches where you need consistent naming conventions.

#### Viewing metadata

Right-click on any image in Picmal and select "Show Metadata" to view detailed information about your images. This includes camera settings, GPS data (if available), color space information, and more.

---

## v1.0.4 - July 16, 2025

### What's New in v1.0.4

- **Metadata Removal Option:** Protect your privacy by removing EXIF data, ICC profiles, GPS coordinates, and other metadata from your images during conversion.
- **Improved Window Resizing:** Better handling of window resizing with smoother animations and more responsive layout adjustments.
- **AVIF Corruption Fix:** Fixed a critical issue where AVIF images could become corrupted during batch conversion processes.

### Privacy-First Metadata Management

This update reinforces Picmal's commitment to privacy. The new metadata removal feature gives you complete control over what information remains in your converted images.

#### What metadata can be removed?

- **EXIF Data:** Camera settings, timestamps, device information
- **GPS Coordinates:** Location data embedded in photos
- **ICC Profiles:** Color management profiles
- **XMP Data:** Adobe metadata and keywords
- **IPTC Data:** Copyright and authorship information

#### Enhanced AVIF Support

AVIF is one of the most efficient modern image formats, offering superior compression compared to JPEG and PNG. This update ensures reliable AVIF conversion, especially important for web developers and content creators working with large image collections.

---

## v1.0.3 - July 11, 2025

### What's New in v1.0.3

- **SVG Format Support:** Convert vector graphics to raster formats while maintaining crisp quality. Perfect for converting icons and illustrations to PNG or JPEG.
- **40% Faster Conversions:** Optimized conversion engine delivers significantly faster processing times, especially noticeable with large batches and high-resolution images.
- **Memory Usage Improvements:** Reduced memory footprint by 30% when processing large images, allowing for smoother operation on older Mac models.

### Performance Improvements

This update focuses on making Picmal faster and more efficient. Whether you're converting a single high-resolution image or processing hundreds of files, you'll notice the improved speed and responsiveness.

#### What's been optimized?

- **Conversion Engine:** Core image processing algorithms have been rewritten for better performance
- **Memory Management:** More efficient handling of large files reduces system impact
- **Batch Processing:** Parallel processing for multiple files when system resources allow
- **UI Responsiveness:** Interface remains smooth even during intensive conversion tasks

#### New SVG Support

Vector graphics are now supported as input format. This is particularly useful for designers who need to convert SVG icons or illustrations to raster formats for different use cases.

**Supported SVG Features:**

- Basic shapes and paths
- Text elements (converted to outlines)
- Gradients and solid fills
- Stroke properties
`;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead
      title={`Changelog - ${SITE_TITLE}`}
      description="Stay updated with the latest Picmal updates, new features, and improvements in our changelog."
    />
    <style>
      /* Staggered fade-in for version entries */
      .version-entry {
        animation: fade-in-up 600ms ease-out backwards;
      }

      .version-entry:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: 100ms; }
      .version-entry:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 150ms; }
      .version-entry:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 200ms; }
      .version-entry:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 250ms; }
      .version-entry:nth-child(5) { animation-delay: 300ms; }
      .version-entry:nth-child(n+6) { animation-delay: 350ms; }

      /* Reduced motion */
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .version-entry {
          animation: none !important;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-background text-text min-h-dvh">
    <Header />

    <main class="relative z-10 pt-32 pb-20">
      <!-- Hero -->
      <div class="text-center mb-16 px-6 animate-fade-in-up">
        <H1 class="mb-4">Changelog</H1>
        <Paragraph class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          Latest updates, new features, and improvements to Picmal.
        </Paragraph>
      </div>

      <!-- Review CTA -->
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 mb-16 animate-fade-in-up stagger-1">
        <div
          class="relative bg-background-subtle border border-border rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-7 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4 sm:gap-6"
        >
          <Paragraph class="mb-0 flex-1">
            As an indie developer, Picmal grows through word of mouth. A review only takes a minute and makes a huge difference.
          </Paragraph>
          <a
            href="https://tally.so/r/Me18qE"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 bg-accent text-white font-semibold text-sm rounded-lg transition-all duration-200 hover:bg-accent-dark hover:scale-[1.02] focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent whitespace-nowrap w-full sm:w-auto"
          >
            Leave a Review
            <svg
              xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
              width="14"
              height="14"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="2.5"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <path d="M5 12h14"></path>
              <path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path>
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Changelog -->
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-20">
        <div class="changelog-wrapper" set:html={changelogContent} />
      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer />

    <script>
      // Transform markdown content into timeline cards
      document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
        const wrapper = document.querySelector('.changelog-wrapper');
        if (!wrapper) return;

        const content = wrapper.innerHTML;
        const entries: string[] = [];
        let currentEntry = '';

        // Split by h2 (version headers)
        const parts = content.split(/(<h2[^>]*>.*?<\/h2>)/);

        for (let i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) {
          const part = parts[i].trim();
          if (!part) continue;

          if (part.startsWith('<h2')) {
            if (currentEntry) {
              entries.push(currentEntry);
            }
            currentEntry = part;
          } else if (currentEntry) {
            currentEntry += part;
          }
        }

        if (currentEntry) {
          entries.push(currentEntry);
        }

        // Transform entries into timeline cards
        const cards = entries.map(entry => {
          const h2Match = entry.match(/<h2[^>]*>(.*?)<\/h2>/);
          if (!h2Match) return '';

          const headerText = h2Match[1];
          const versionMatch = headerText.match(/v?[\d.]+/);
          const dateMatch = headerText.match(/\w+ \d+, \d+/);

          const version = versionMatch ? versionMatch[0] : '';
          const date = dateMatch ? dateMatch[0] : '';

          let contentHtml = entry
            .replace(/<h2[^>]*>.*?<\/h2>/, '')
            .replace(/<hr\s*\/?>/g, '')
            .trim();

          return `
            <div class="version-entry mb-12">
              <div class="bg-background-subtle border border-border rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-7">
                <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3 mb-5 flex-wrap">
                  <span class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text tracking-tight">${version}</span>
                  <span class="text-sm text-text-secondary">${date}</span>
                </div>
                <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:text-text prose-headings:font-semibold prose-p:text-text-secondary prose-p:leading-relaxed prose-h3:text-xl prose-h3:mb-3 prose-h4:text-base prose-h4:mb-2 prose-a:text-accent prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline prose-img:rounded-lg prose-img:my-6 prose-img:shadow-lg prose-img:border prose-img:border-border prose-video:rounded-lg prose-video:my-6 prose-video:shadow-lg prose-li:text-text-secondary prose-li:leading-relaxed prose-ul:space-y-2 prose-strong:text-text prose-strong:font-semibold prose-code:text-accent prose-code:bg-accent/10 prose-code:px-1.5 prose-code:py-0.5 prose-code:rounded prose-pre:bg-background-subtle prose-pre:border prose-pre:border-border prose-blockquote:border-l-accent prose-blockquote:text-text-secondary prose-blockquote:bg-background-subtle/50">
                  ${contentHtml}
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          `;
        }).join('');

        wrapper.innerHTML = cards;
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
